// deterministic fallback built exactly that shape for demonstrative targets, because
// mandarinFallbackPair files 这个/那个 as partOfSpeech 'pronoun' and hands them the
// personal-pronoun frames at §69 (那个 + 想 + VERB, 那个 + VERB). The shipped results were
// 那个想可以。 ("that want can" — zh-daily-run2, accepted at its 11th check, and the reason that
// run ended one recall short), 这个想喝。 (shipped in the only READY run of the v676 benchmark)
// and 这个想吃。.
//
// These were NOT accepted through a fallback bypass. They went through the same
// validateMandarinPair that every model candidate goes through, and it had no rule for them.
// So the rule goes HERE, in the shared surface-grammar checks, where both origins meet it.
//
// Deliberately narrow, to catch the proven malformations without rejecting correct Chinese:
//   (a) demonstrative + 想/要 + verb     — stacked volitional with an inanimate agent
//   (b) demonstrative + verb + nothing   — no object and no following content at all
// A demonstrative followed by a noun (这个东西…), an adjective (这个很大), a question word
// (这个怎么做？), a stative/modal predicate (这个可以。) or a pronoun subject (这个我想喝。) is
